WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Wednesday,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.360
the twenty-fifth of November.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.400
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.360
Four more ships have been attacked
around the Strait of Hormuz,

5
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.000
and a marine insurer is now telling
owners to avoid non-essential transits.

6
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.600
Even so, crude is trading
near three-month lows.

7
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.440
Iraq is disputing its OPEC plus
capacity assessment ahead of Sunday's

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.520
meeting, and European gas storage
is falling at its fastest pace this

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.480
month.

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.600
On the markets. Early Tuesday, Brent
was at eighty-eight dollars seventy

11
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.800
a barrel, with West Texas Intermediate
at seventy-nine dollars sixty.

12
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.640
Both were near three-month lows,
according to OilPrice dot com.

13
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.280
The Dutch Title Transfer
Facility front-month,

14
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.360
Europe's gas benchmark, topped
ninety euros fifty a megawatt hour,

15
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.560
its fourth straight session of gains.

16
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.520
EU gas storage stood at sixty-eight
point four percent on the twenty-third

17
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.560
of November, according to
Gas Infrastructure Europe.

18
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.960
Starting in the Gulf. Four more
commercial vessels were hit in and around

19
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.480
the Strait of Hormuz, and tugboats
are now among the targets,

20
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.640
gCaptain reported. That takes its
running count of reported tanker strikes

21
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.360
to ten. The outlet frames this
as Iran widening its crackdown.

22
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:17.360
Separately, Iran says three
tankers struck mines in the strait.

23
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.187
That claim has not been
independently confirmed.

24
00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.920
The reports also don't name the ships,
their cargoes or the damage from

25
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.560
the four new attacks.

26
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.320
Shipowners are responding.

27
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.440
The Swedish Club, a marine insurer,
now advises against non-essential

28
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.040
transits, citing attacks, congestion
and navigational interference.

29
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.600
With fewer owners willing to go
through, demand piles onto the ships

30
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.400
that will. Fifteen-year-old very large
crude carriers are now worth considerably

31
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.880
more than newbuilds.

32
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.040
Gas carriers are just as tight.

33
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.600
Earnings for very large gas carriers
on the Ras Tanura to Chiba route

34
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.200
are high enough to pull ethane
carriers into liquefied petroleum gas

35
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.880
trades, according to the Baltic Exchange.

36
00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.680
The US is also looking into whether
Iran was behind cyberattacks on up

37
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.840
to fifty tankers, the Wall
Street Journal reported.

38
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.400
That is a probe with no findings yet.

39
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.960
Crude has barely priced any of this.

40
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.027
Oil did close higher on Tuesday as
the attacks overshadowed diplomacy,

41
00:02:14.053 --> 00:02:17.000
Rigzone reported, though
no figure was given.

42
00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.800
Over to OPEC plus, which meets on Sunday.

43
00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.360
Baghdad rejects an assessment that
it can sustainably produce less than

44
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.080
five million barrels a day.

45
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.240
It wants about six million
recognised before the meeting,

46
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.680
where targets for twenty twenty-seven
are expected to be discussed,

47
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.280
according to OilPrice dot com.

48
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.080
Iraq's current limit is just over
four point four million barrels a day.

49
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.080
A higher capacity baseline would
give it a case for more quota room,

50
00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.080
and that comes in a market forecasters
already see tipping into surplus.

51
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.960
Baghdad is also seeking federal
control of North Oil Company fields in

52
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.120
Kurdistan, after the oil minister
said an investigation found smuggling

53
00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:55.740
there.

54
00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.240
Saudi Arabia, meanwhile, now expects
its economy to shrink two point

55
00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.400
one percent this year, down from
a forecast of three point six.

56
00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.960
That's according to its budget statement.

57
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.000
October exports were the
highest since the war began,

58
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.520
with Aramco sending more crude west
through the East-West pipeline to

59
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.960
Yanbu.

60
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.760
Turning to European gas. Storage fell
half a percentage point in a single

61
00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.160
day, from sixty-eight point nine percent
on the twenty-second of November.

62
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.760
The gains in prices came
as a cold snap set in.

63
00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.760
In its October report, the Gas Exporting
Countries Forum put the benchmark

64
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.920
up twelve percent on the month.

65
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.160
Year on year, it was up one
hundred and sixty-three percent.

66
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.600
Asia may soon compete
harder for the same cargoes.

67
00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.440
Japan's physical spark spread has
turned positive on a seven-day average

68
00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.560
for the first time since the
war began, Bloomberg reported.

69
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.800
Gas-fired power is profitable again there.

70
00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.840
If Japanese utilities buy more
spot liquefied natural gas,

71
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.280
they'd be bidding against Europe
for Atlantic cargoes just as storage

72
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.480
draws down.

73
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.360
For the longer term, Equinor agreed
an eighteen-year deal to supply VNG

74
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.920
in Germany, starting
in twenty twenty-seven,

75
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.280
according to Offshore Energy.

76
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.480
Back to oil, where crude and products
are telling different stories.

77
00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.440
Brent has fallen more than
twenty percent in November,

78
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.200
but diesel remains tight even
after recent declines in margins,

79
00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.280
OilPrice dot com reported.

80
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.600
US retail diesel dropped below
six dollars a gallon last week.

81
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.000
Cheap crude is drawing buyers.

82
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.520
Chinese state and independent refiners
have stepped up purchases this

83
00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.880
month to refill stocks,
according to Rigzone.

84
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.320
South Korea's trade ministry says
it has secured November and December

85
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.440
crude at ninety percent
of last year's levels.

86
00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.400
For January, it's seventy-five percent.

87
00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.000
A few more things.

88
00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.680
Ukraine's president, Volodymyr
Zelenskiy, said Ukraine carried out a

89
00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.360
drone strike on a Russian cargo
ship in the Gulf of Finland.

90
00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.600
Russia's response hasn't been reported.

91
00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.120
Ukraine's foreign minister called
the weekend strike in Libyan waters

92
00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.920
self-defence, after
criticism from Tripoli.

93
00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.080
The European Commission's proposed
twenty-second sanctions package would

94
00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.080
ban tankers insured in Russia.

95
00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.120
It's a proposal only and
has not been adopted.

96
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.440
Petrobras raised its five-year
spending plan by twelve percent,

97
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.000
to one hundred and
twenty-two billion dollars.

98
00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.400
ExxonMobil took a four billion dollar
final investment decision to extend

99
00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.120
output from Block fifteen offshore Angola.

100
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.520
It also announced the block's
twenty-first discovery.

101
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.880
Brava Energia is taking full ownership
and operatorship of the Pescada

102
00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.680
cluster from Petrobras,
with no cash payment.

103
00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:42.160
In Iran, President Pezeshkian warned
on Saturday the twenty-first of

104
00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.080
winter gas supply problems after
attacks on gas infrastructure.

105
00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.480
And the US Senate is investigating
Vice President Vance's alleged ties

106
00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.320
to Vitol over a Venezuela oil contract.

107
00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.680
What to watch next. Daily EU gas
storage readings through the second

108
00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.160
of December, as the cold snap goes on.

109
00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.040
The OPEC plus meeting on
Sunday, the twenty-ninth,

110
00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.520
with targets for twenty twenty-seven
and Iraq's capacity claim on the

111
00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:10.960
